    {
      "number": 72,
      "title": "Fable commander: reconcile LIMS outputs across clinical and water/public-utility lanes",
      "url": "https://github.com/TombStoneDash/lims-box/issues/72",
      "body": "## Purpose\n\nUse one bounded Fable 5 commander pass to reconcile all existing LIMS BOX/LIMS BOT Fable outputs, specs, proof and current repo state, then execute the useful delta. Do not create another general roadmap.\n\n## Scope\n\nReconcile across the related LIMS repositories and canonical product truth:\n\n- `TombStoneDash/lims-box`;\n- `TombStoneDash/limsbot`;\n- `TombStoneDash/lims-bot-demo` where relevant;\n- clinical/public-health laboratory product and revenue work;\n- water, wastewater, environmental and public-utility laboratory opportunities;\n- issue #70 duplicate Vercel project/domain reconciliation;\n- demo, pricing, early-access, analytics, CRM/outreach packets and current production proof;\n- all accessible prior Fable/Claude outputs and abandoned implementation packets.\n\n## Fable work\n\n1. classify outputs as DONE, ACTIVE, BUILD_NOW, TRUE_GATE, SUPERSEDED, DUPLICATE, HOLD or KILL;\n2. identify one clinical-lab revenue lane and one water/public-utility revenue lane;\n3. preserve current repos/domains and avoid duplicate product surfaces;\n4. produce no more than five bounded Sonnet/Codex packets;\n5. dispatch machine-safe implementation, tests, demo and reconciliation work immediately.\n\nUse Fable for cross-file/product synthesis, market/offer judgment and contradictory-plan resolution. Use Sonnet/Codex for code, tests, PRs, demo preparation, data-safe CRM tooling and domain/project inventory.\n\n## Stops\n\nNo protected LIMS outbound send, payment, contract, production database mutation, DNS/domain transfer, secret mutation or project deletion without the named gate. Read-only production checks, repo work, draft outreach assets, event/opportunity research and PR creation are not gates.\n\n## Terminal output\n\nReturn only verified current state, stale/duplicate outputs rejected, clinical lane, water/public-utility lane, work dispatched/completed, true gates, proof and next automatic actions."
    },
    {
      "number": 94,
      "title": "Restore automatic Personnel Pack PDF fulfillment",
      "url": "https://github.com/TombStoneDash/lims-box/issues/94",
      "body": "## Incident\n\nA production Personnel Pack request on 2026-08-26 was captured, but the internal fallback notice reported that no PDF URL is configured and manual fulfillment is required.\n\nNo applicant name, email address, organization, or request-specific PII is included here.\n\n## Impact\n\n- lead capture succeeds;\n- the applicant does not receive the requested Personnel Pack automatically;\n- support must acknowledge and fulfill each request manually;\n- a configured accreditation selection cannot produce a verified download.\n\n## Containment completed\n\nThe affected applicant received one manual acknowledgment from Tombstone Dash Gmail. Do not send a duplicate acknowledgment.\n\n## Required repair\n\n1. Identify the intended source-of-truth Personnel Pack PDF for each supported accreditation type.\n2. Verify each asset contains only approved public/demo content and no customer data.\n3. Configure the production download URL through the existing secret/configuration path.\n4. Make the applicant confirmation include a working, access-controlled or public download as intended.\n5. Add regression coverage for configured and missing-PDF behavior.\n6. Run one production-safe external-inbox test proving the confirmation and download both work.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- supported accreditation selections map to approved assets;\n- no fallback/manual-fulfillment notice on the test;\n- external confirmation arrives once;\n- download returns the intended PDF;\n- no applicant PII appears in issues, fixtures, logs, or receipts;\n- production proof is timestamped before closure."
    },
    {
      "number": 95,
      "title": "Audit inactive Google OAuth clients before deletion",
      "url": "https://github.com/TombStoneDash/lims-box/issues/95",
      "body": "## Alert\n\nGoogle Developers reported on 2026-08-27 that the `lims-box` Google Cloud project has OAuth clients inactive for at least five months and scheduled for automatic deletion in 30 days.\n\nNo client IDs, secrets, account data, or customer information are included here.\n\n## Required work\n\n1. Inventory the inactive OAuth clients in the `lims-box` Google Cloud project.\n2. Map each client to its current production, preview, local, or retired use without exposing credentials.\n3. For every client still required, exercise it through a legitimate Sign in with Google flow or refresh-token exchange before the deadline.\n4. Allow truly retired clients to expire or remove them deliberately.\n5. Verify current LIMS BOX authentication in production and the supported development environment after the audit.\n6. Record privacy-safe proof and the final keep/retire disposition for each client.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Every listed inactive client has one owner and a keep/retire decision.\n- Required clients are exercised before 2026-09-26 and remain valid.\n- Retired clients are not referenced by deployed configuration.\n- Production authentication is verified without logging tokens, client secrets, or user PII."
    }
